{"name":"Highlight Gold","hex":"#dfc16d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"highlight","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An area or a spot in a drawing, painting, or photograph that is strongly illuminated.","An especially significant or interesting detail or event or period of time."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make prominent; emphasize.","To be a highlight of."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/highlight"},{"term":"gold","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A heavy yellow elemental metal of great value, with atomic number 79.","A coin or coinage made of this material, or supposedly so."]},{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["☉ (alchemy)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gold"}],"entries":[{"title":"Highlight (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Highlight, formerly known as Beast, is a South Korean boy band formed by Cube Entertainment. The band consists of four members: Yoon Doo-joon, Yang Yo-seob, Lee Gi-kwang, and Son Dong-woon. Highlight was originally a six-piece band; Jang Hyun-seung departed from the group in April 2016, and Yong Jun-hyung departed in March 2019. In late 2016, the group moved labels from Cube Entertainment to Around Us Entertainment and subsequently changed their name to Highlight in 2017."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Highlight_at_G-KPOP_2022.jpg/330px-Highlight_at_G-KPOP_2022.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Highlight_(band)","wikidata":"Q269595"},{"title":"Gold","blocks":[{"text":"Gold is a chemical element; its chemical symbol is Au and atomic number 79. In its pure form, it is a bright-metallic-yellow, dense, soft, malleable, and ductile metal. Chemically, gold is a transition metal, a group 11 element, and one of the noble metals. It is one of the least reactive chemical elements, being the second lowest in the reactivity series, with only platinum ranked as less reactive. Gold is solid under standard conditions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Gold-crystals.jpg/330px-Gold-crystals.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold","wikidata":"Q897"},{"title":"Gold (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Gold, also called golden, is a color tone resembling the chemical element gold."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg/330px-GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold_(color)","wikidata":"Q208045"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Beast_at_Lotte_Giants_2010_Special_Concert_100321.jpg/500px-Beast_at_Lotte_Giants_2010_Special_Concert_100321.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Beast_at_Lotte_Giants_2010_Special_Concert_100321.jpg/500px-Beast_at_Lotte_Giants_2010_Special_Concert_100321.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Beast performing in 2010.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABeast_at_Lotte_Giants_2010_Special_Concert_100321.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/BEAST_at_the_Expo_2012_Yeosu.JPG/500px-BEAST_at_the_Expo_2012_Yeosu.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/BEAST_at_the_Expo_2012_Yeosu.JPG/500px-BEAST_at_the_Expo_2012_Yeosu.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Beast performing at the Expo 2012.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABEAST_at_the_Expo_2012_Yeosu.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/14.11.23_%EB%A9%9C%EB%A1%A0_%EB%AE%A4%EC%A7%81_%EC%96